ck_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105801","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105801","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105801.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105801.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-24T15:10:46Z"},"body":"Initially I [suggested](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/91006#pullrequestreview-2791750125) deprecating these functions, but now I think it makes sense to have shorthands for simple scenarios. We just need to add a reference to `Engine.capture_script_backtraces()` for advanced scenarios.\r\n\r\n* Remove the restriction on using these functions only in the main thread. This already works for `Engine.capture_script_backtraces()`, since the stack information is stored in `thread_local` variables.\r\n* Update documentation. These functions and `Engine.capture_script_backtraces()` use the same mechanism, so the same rules apply to them.\r\n* Add stack output to `Utils.check()`, see the [comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96229#issuecomment-2316077908).\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends EditorScript\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n    var thread := Thread.new()\r\n    thread.start(_thread_function)\r\n    test()\r\n    thread.wait_to_finish()\r\n\r\nfunc _thread_function() -> void:\r\n    test()\r\n\r\nfunc test() -> void:\r\n    #print_stack()\r\n    #print(Engine.capture_script_backtraces())\r\n    for i in 10:\r\n        prints(i, get_stack().slice(1))\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repit